1
00:06:15,555 --> 00:06:21,555
Mankind was born on Earth. It was never meant to die here.

2
00:12:31,111 --> 00:12:37,111
Interstellar is a adventure, drama, science fiction
film directed by Christopher Nolan.

3
00:18:46,666 --> 00:18:52,666
The adventures of a group of explorers who make use of a newly discovered wormhole to surpass the
limitations on human space travel and conquer the vast distances involved in an interstellar voyage.

4
00:25:02,222 --> 00:25:08,222
Cooper, played by Matthew McConaughey.

5
00:31:17,777 --> 00:31:23,777
Brand, played by Anne Hathaway.

6
00:37:33,333 --> 00:37:39,333
Professor Brand, played by Michael Caine.

7
00:43:48,888 --> 00:43:54,888
Murph, played by Jessica Chastain.

8
00:50:04,444 --> 00:50:10,444
Tom, played by Casey Affleck.

9
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
Doyle, played by Wes Bentley.

10
01:02:35,555 --> 01:02:41,555
Interstellar is a 2014 epic science fiction film directed by Christopher Nolan,
who co-wrote the screenplay with his brother Jonathan Nolan.

11
01:08:51,111 --> 01:08:57,111
It features an ensemble cast led by Matthew McConaughey, Anne Hathaway,
Jessica Chastain, Bill Irwin, Ellen Burstyn, and Michael Caine.

12
01:15:06,666 --> 01:15:12,666
Set in a dystopian future where Earth is suffering from catastrophic blight and famine, the film follows a
group of astronauts who travel through a wormhole near Saturn in search of a new home for mankind.

13
01:21:22,222 --> 01:21:28,222
The screenplay had its origins in a script that Jonathan had developed in
2007 and was originally set to be directed by Steven Spielberg.

14
01:27:37,777 --> 01:27:43,777
Theoretical physicist Kip Thorne was an executive producer and scientific consultant
on the film, and wrote the tie-in book The Science of Interstellar.

15
01:33:53,333 --> 01:33:59,333
It was Lynda Obst's final film as producer before her death.

16
01:40:08,888 --> 01:40:14,888
Cinematographer Hoyte van Hoytema shot it on 35 mm film in the
Panavision anamorphic format and IMAX 70 mm.

17
01:46:24,444 --> 01:46:30,444
Filming began in late 2013 and took place in Alberta, Klaustur, and Los Angeles.

18
01:52:40,000 --> 01:52:46,000
Interstellar uses extensive practical and miniature effects, and
the company DNEG created additional visual effects.

19
01:58:55,555 --> 01:59:01,555
Interstellar premiered at the TCL Chinese Theatre on October 26, 2014, and was released in theaters in the United States on November
5, and in the United Kingdom on November 7, with Paramount Pictures distributing in the United States and Warner Bros.

20
02:05:11,111 --> 02:05:17,111
Pictures distributing in international markets.

21
02:11:26,666 --> 02:11:32,666
In the United States, it was first released on film stock,
expanding to venues using digital projectors.

22
02:17:42,222 --> 02:17:48,222
It was a commercial success, grossing $681 million worldwide during its initial theatrical run, and $773.8
million worldwide with subsequent releases, making it the 10th-highest-grossing film of 2014.

23
02:23:57,777 --> 02:24:03,777
The film received generally positive reviews from critics.

24
02:30:13,333 --> 02:30:19,333
Among its various accolades, Interstellar was nominated for five awards
at the 87th Academy Awards, winning Best Visual Effects.

25
02:36:28,888 --> 02:36:34,888
The film explores themes of rescue, future, spacecraft, race
against time, artificial intelligence (a.i.).

26
02:42:44,444 --> 02:42:50,444
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
